#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# max_value

#% text
# `max_value(f, x)` gives the global maximum value of `f`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It is the first part of `maximize(f, x)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A downward parabola:

#% cell
max_value(1 - x^2, x)
#% output
#= 1

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# On an interval:

#% cell
max_value([x*(1 - x), 0 <= x and x <= 1], x)
#% output
#= 1/4

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `maximize` gives the point too:

#% cell
maximize(1 - x^2, x)
#% output
#= [1, [x -> 0]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `maximize`, `min_value`, `arg_max`
